  "prefLabel": "Env-Wq 1108.10 Cross-Connection Control",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Wq 1108.10 Cross-Connection Control. The owner of a PBF shall ensure that:\n\n(a) Water service to the PBF is protected against backflow and back siphonage;\n\n(b) Water introduced to the PBF, whether directly or through the circulation system, is supplied through an air gap of at least 6 inches; and\n\n(c) Vacuum breaker backflow preventers are installed prior to all hose bibs servicing the PBF.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1100) #8468, eff 11-1-05; ss by #10577, eff 5-1-14 (See Revision Note #2 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1100); ss by #13198, eff 5-1-21 (see Revision Note #3 at chapter heading for Env-Wq 1100) (formerly Env-Wq 1105.10)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-wq1100.html"
